-- ============================================================================
-- DR7 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Cementing, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: whether the mud got out of the way. Cement takes the
-- WIDE side of an eccentric annulus, because resistance in a slot goes as the
-- inverse cube of the gap, and it leaves the narrow side as a channel that
-- shows up decades later as sustained casing pressure or a failed
-- abandonment. Standoff is the narrow gap over the concentric clearance, which
-- is 0.019049999999999997 m in this well's open hole and 0.021348699999999998
-- in the cased section. A bow spring is a SPRING and a rigid centralizer is a
-- SPACER, and the spring rate has the CLEARANCE inside it, so one device has
-- different rates in different hole sizes: 1415732.124393542 N per metre in
-- the open hole and 1263294.5785784135 in the cased one.
--
-- THE FINDING THE TIER IS BUILT ON. The centralizer is not what binds. The
-- deflection at a centralizer is LINEAR in the spacing and the mid-span sag is
-- QUARTIC, and on both published wells the reported minimum standoff is the
-- mid-span value at every interval. On the horizontal well the value at the
-- centralizer is 0.8462214846722909, which passes the API 67 percent target
-- comfortably, and the reported 0.599178961025609, which is the mid-span
-- value, fails it. A design conversation that stopped at the centralizer would
-- have signed that job off. Tripling the restoring force from 8900 to 26700 N
-- buys 10.3 points; dropping the spacing from 12 m to 9 buys 20.7, because the
-- spring does nothing at all to the sag. And the sag-only ceiling at 12 m and
-- 90 degrees is 0.7529574763533182, which no bow spring can exceed at any
-- cost.
--
-- A SECOND FINDING. The same centralizer programme at 12 m passes on the slant
-- well at 0.742357202445576 and FAILS on the horizontal one. Their required
-- spacings, bisected, are 13.05523892558449 m and 11.187558579905271, and the
-- job runs 12 on both. The two wells differ only in inclination: a lateral
-- load 1.5557238268604126 times larger, which needs the centralizers only
-- 1.1669426204421298 times closer, because the fourth power that made the
-- problem steep also makes the remedy cheap. The standoff reaches exactly ZERO
-- at 17.021127200569346 m of spacing at 90 degrees, and that is the sag
-- reaching the whole clearance rather than the centralizer bottoming out,
-- which would need 78.03430781229383 m.
--
-- A THIRD, AND IT IS A DECISION THE ENGINE MAKES SILENTLY. standoffProfile
-- runs annulusRows with an excess of ZERO, so the volume side of this course
-- measures the open hole at 0.22104932820526735 m and the centralization side
-- at the nominal 0.2159. There is a real argument for it, the error it makes
-- is OPTIMISTIC, and it is much worse for a rigid blade than for a bow spring:
-- a 0.206 m blade drops from 0.7401574803149601 to 0.6520332493064135 in the
-- washed-out hole, with no spring to take up the slack.
--
-- AND THE CHECKLIST HAS NO PERCENTAGE ON IT, which is a design decision the
-- engine states in its own comment: honest, not a fake efficiency percentage.
-- Five items, each true or false, each carrying the number that decided it,
-- because the weights in a score would be invented, a score hides which item
-- failed, and no field measurement ever returns one.
--
-- WHAT THIS TIER TEACHES AND CERTIFIES NOWHERE: casing rotation and
-- reciprocation, intermixing and contamination, thickening time and
-- compressive strength, temperature, losses to the formation, gas migration
-- after placement, the transient free-fall rate, tension times dogleg in the
-- standoff, and cement bond evaluation.
-- 20260830_dr7_cementing_go_live.sql asserts it.
--
-- Numeric sweep and tier-leakage sweep as for the tiers below: 0 unresolved
-- literals, 0 downward leaks, 0 same-tier answer prints.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

